  <div class="accordion_group component_block layout_in_content accordion_compact">
    
<div class="accordion_item component_item">
  <button class="accordion_trigger" aria-expanded="false">Advocacy / Community Service</button>
  <div class="accordion_body typography" role="region" aria-hidden="true" hidden>
    <p><strong>Advocacy/Service Groups</strong>&nbsp;serve others. Some groups partner with local schools, free clinics, or other nonprofits to provide ongoing outreach and service. Many groups target particular communities or health conditions. Several do broader or national advocacy work in health policy or other issues.</p><ul><li>Breeze Against Wheeze</li><li>Brown Human Rights Asylum Clinic (BHRAC)</li><li>CATCH</li><li>Clinica Esperanza/Hope Clinic</li><li>Community Health Advocacy Program (CHAP)</li><li>Eating Disorder Awareness</li><li>Environmental Coalition of The Warren Alpert Medical School (ECo)</li><li>Full Swing Golf Rhode Island</li><li>Giving A Boost</li><li>Habitat for Humanity @ Brown Med</li><li>Lion's Club Eye Clinic</li><li>MagicAid</li><li>Med Wheels</li><li>Medical Optimization Group @ WAMS</li><li>Medical Students for Choice (MSFC)</li><li>NORD Students for Rare</li><li>Rest With Dignity</li><li>Rhode Island Free Clinic</li><li>Rhode Island Medical Navigator Partnership (RIMNP)</li><li>Rhode Island Medical Society</li><li>Sex Ed at Brown Med</li><li>Stop the Bleed Rhode Island</li><li>Teddy Bear Clinic</li><li><p>Transitions of Care Workshops</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p>
  </div>
</div>


  
<div class="accordion_item component_item">
  <button class="accordion_trigger" aria-expanded="false">Affinity</button>
  <div class="accordion_body typography" role="region" aria-hidden="true" hidden>
    <p><strong>Affinity Groups</strong> provide opportunities for students to engage in community service and/or public health advocacy.</p><ul><li>American Medical Women’s Association (AMWA)</li><li>American Muslim Medical Student Association (AMMSA)</li><li>Asian Pacific American Medical Student Association (APAMSA)</li><li>Catholic Medical Association</li><li>Filipino Americans in Medicine at Brown University (FAM@Brown)</li><li>First Gen Med @ Brown</li><li>JeMSA</li><li>Latino Medical Student Association</li><li>Medical Student Pride Alliance (MSPA)</li><li>Medical Students with Disability and Chronic Illness</li><li>NAAMA (National Arab American Medical Association)</li><li>South Asian Medical Students Association (SAMSA)</li><li>Student National Medical Association (SNMA)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p>
  </div>
</div>


  
<div class="accordion_item component_item">
  <button class="accordion_trigger" aria-expanded="false">Arts &amp; Innovation</button>
  <div class="accordion_body typography" role="region" aria-hidden="true" hidden>
    <p><strong>Arts and Innovations Groups</strong> provide opportunities that encourage creativity, interdisciplinary thinking, and/or the integration of the arts into medical education and practice.</p><ul><li>Create@Brown</li><li>Design x Health</li><li>Medical Records (a capella)</li><li>Plexus Literary Magazine</li></ul>
  </div>
</div>


  
<div class="accordion_item component_item">
  <button class="accordion_trigger" aria-expanded="false">Medical Association Chapters</button>
  <div class="accordion_body typography" role="region" aria-hidden="true" hidden>
    <p><strong>Medical Association Representative Groups&nbsp;</strong>serve as local chapters of national medical associations.</p><ul><li>Aerospace Medicine</li><li>American Association of Neurological Surgeons Medical Student Chapter of the Warren Alpert Medical School</li><li>American Medical Association</li><li>Association of Women Surgeons (AWS)</li><li>Brown University Local Chapter of the American Physician Scientists Association (Brown University APSA Chapter)</li><li>Global Surgery Student Alliance</li><li>Mission: Brain</li><li>The Hippocratic Society (Warren Alpert Medical School University Chapter)</li><li><p>Women’s Orthopedic Leadership Forum / Ruth Jackson Orthopedic Society (WOLF)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p></li></ul>
  </div>
</div>


  
<div class="accordion_item component_item">
  <button class="accordion_trigger" aria-expanded="false">Specialty Interest Groups</button>
  <div class="accordion_body typography" role="region" aria-hidden="true" hidden>
    <p><strong>Specialty Interest Groups</strong>&nbsp;provide forums or students to explore specific specialties, including opportunities to learn about career pathways, gain relevant knowledge and skills, and connect to specialty-specific mentors.</p><ul><li>Anesthesiology Interest Group</li><li>Brown General Surgery Society</li><li>Cardiology Interest Group</li><li>Cardiothoracic Surgery Specialty Interest Group</li><li>Cerebrovascular Student Alliance</li><li>Child and Adolescent Psychiatry Interest Group (CAPIG)</li><li>Dermatology Interest Group</li><li>Diagnostic Radiology Interest Group</li><li>Emergency Medicine &amp; Critical Care Interest Group</li><li>ENT Specialty Interest Group</li><li>Family Medicine Interest Group</li><li>Gastroenterology Specialty Interest Group</li><li>Infectious Disease and Immunology Interest Group</li><li>Internal Medicine Interest Group</li><li>Interventional Radiology Interest Group</li><li>Lifestyle Medicine Interest Group</li><li>Med-Peds Interest Group</li><li>Neurology and Neurosurgery Interest Group</li><li>Obstetrics and Gynecology Interest Group</li><li>Ophthalmology Interest Group (OIG)</li><li>Orthopedics Specialty Interest Group</li><li>Pediatrics Interest Group</li><li>Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation (PM&amp;R) Student Interest Group</li><li>Plastic Surgery Specialty Interest Group</li><li>Psychiatry Student Interest Group (Mind &amp; Brain)</li><li>Sports Medicine (Orthopedics surgery or Primary Care Sports Medicine)</li><li>Ultrasound Interest Group</li><li>Urology Specialty Interest Group</li><li>Vascular Surgery Interest Group</li></ul>
  </div>
</div>


  
<div class="accordion_item component_item">
  <button class="accordion_trigger" aria-expanded="false">Student Life and Recreation</button>
  <div class="accordion_body typography" role="region" aria-hidden="true" hidden>
    <p><strong>Student Life / Recreation Groups</strong>&nbsp;offer opportunities for students to build community through shared interests and recreational activities that support balance and connection.</p><ul><li>Climbing Club</li><li>Code Dink</li><li>Medical Cycle Association</li><li><p>Medical School Ski and Snowboard Group</p><p>&nbsp;</p></li></ul>
  </div>
</div>


  
<div class="accordion_item component_item">
  <button class="accordion_trigger" aria-expanded="false">Well-Being</button>
  <div class="accordion_body typography" role="region" aria-hidden="true" hidden>
    <p><strong>Well-Being Groups</strong> promote student well-being through advocacy, support mechanism, mentorship, and/or educational initiatives.</p><ul><li>Als Pals</li><li>Book WA(r)MS</li><li>Med²</li><li>Medical Humanities Initiative</li><li>Serotonin Seekers of Rhode Island Run Club (SSRIs)</li><li>Student Health Council (SHC)&nbsp;</li></ul>
  </div>
</div>



</div>


<div class="wysiwyg_block">
  <div class="wysiwyg_block_inner">
    <div class="typography">
        <p>Please contact the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.brown.edu/academics/medical-old/student-affairs/senate/">Student Senate</a>&nbsp;(<a href="mailto:ams-senate@brown.edu">ams-senate@brown.edu</a>) or the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.brown.edu/academics/medical/student-affairs">Office of Student Affairs</a>&nbsp;(<a href="mailto:medstudentaffairs@brown.edu">medstudentaffairs@brown.edu</a>) with any questions about student groups. &nbsp;</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


              

                            
                            
                            
                            
